{title: 272 - Give Me the Bible}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #272 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 272}
{meta: category Holy Scriptures - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Give me the Bible, [D]star of gladness [G]gleaming,
[C]To cheer the wand'rer [G]lone and tempest [D]tossed;
[G]No storm can hide that radiance [D]peaceful [G]beaming,
[C]Since Jesus came to [D]seek and save the [G]lost.
[G]Give me the Bible, holy message [C]shining;
[G]Thy light shall guide me in the [A]narrow [D]way;
[G]Precept and promise, [D]law and love com[G]bining,
[C]Till night shall vanish [D]in eternal [G]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Give [D]me [G]the Bible--
[C]holy [G]message [D]shining,
[G]Thy [D]light shall [G]guide me
[C]in [D]the [G]narrow way.
[G]Precept [C]and promise,
[G]law [A]and [D]love combining,
[G]'Til [D]night [G]shall vanish
[C]in [D]eternal [G]day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Give [D]me [G]the Bible
[C]when [G]my heart [D]is broken,
[G]When [D]sin and [G]grief have
[C]filled [D]my soul [G]with fear,
[G]Give me [C]the precious
[G]words [A]by [D]Jesus spoken,
[G]Hold [D]up [G]faith's lamp
[C]to [D]show my [G]Savior near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Give [D]me [G]the Bible,
[C]all [G]my [D]steps enlighten,
[G]Teach [D]me [G]the danger
[C]of [D]these [G]realms below,
[G]That lamp [C]of safety,
[G]o'er [A]the gloom [D]shall brighten,
[G]That [D]light [G]alone
[C]the path [D]of peace [G]can show.
{end_of_verse}
